## Checker semantics

The checker tests what test-strategy.md section 5 names:

- P2-a: four batch JSONs plus four logs exist, batches hold 6 to 9 maps, the union holds
  30 unique slugs, and every TSV slug appears in exactly one batch.
- P2-b: each rating is a labeled JSON number in [0, 10] (jq type check, not digit matching),
  with a boolean critical field and a note string.
- P2-c: each batch records a route of provider/model shape, a model_family outside the
  claude/anthropic/sonnet family, a route string with no claude/anthropic name, and a log
  citing the route. This reading agrees with the strategy: the judge family must differ from
  the maker family (Anthropic Sonnet) and the claude family is excluded.
- P2-d: every inventory row holds state cell rated (last cell, awk-parsed) with the copied
  rating and note equal to the batch JSON values (numeric compare).
- A9: the checker reads the live track path, not an archive.

## Live fixture probes (fixture at measure/runs/asset_scenes_civic_20260928/review-a-p2-fixture)

Control run with faithful copies: passes 34/34. Then one mutation per probe:

1. mill Judge critical cell flipped to false -> PASSES 34/34. The gate never reads the cell.
2. mill judge route cell set to anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5 -> PASSES 34/34. The gate never
   reads the inventory route cell.
3. batch b1 model_family Anthropic Sonnet, route anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5 -> FAILS
   P2-c with 3 FAILs (family, route, log citation). A claude-family judge cannot pass.
4. apothecary rating set to the string 2026-11-19 -> FAILS P2-b (labeled number parse) and
   P2-d (copy mismatch). A date cannot pass as a rating.
5. bathhouse dropped from batch b1 -> FAILS with 5 FAILs (rating count 29, unique slug
   count 29, slug in 0 batches, no entry, nothing to copy). A missing deliverable cannot pass.

Probes 3, 4, and 5 re-verify the smoke claims recorded in red-p2.log (fixtures removed there).

## Record verification (beyond the gate)

An independent node cross-check compared all 30 inventory rows with the four batch JSONs on
rating (numeric compare), critical flag, judge note, judge route cell, and state cell rated in
last position: 30 rows, 0 mismatches. The inventory slug set versus the 30 civic P2 TSV slugs
has an empty symmetric difference. All 30 MAPS rating and MAPS note cells are byte-identical to
the Phase 1 inventory at 3e8d29e8: 0 differences. The four batch logs each cite the route and
an explicit model id (kimi-for-coding).

## By-design check-inventory.sh failure

bash measure/runs/asset_scenes_civic_20260928/check-inventory.sh
-> exit 1, === Total: 96 checks (PASS=6, FAIL=90) ===
This matches plan.md:63-64 exactly. The failure is by design: the Phase 1 checker asserts
judge: no and state inventoried, which a rated row no longer holds. Gap for later gates: the
Phase 1 closeout rerun stays red forever (its acceptance is pinned at 3e8d29e8, so the record
is intact), and check-review.sh P2-d will fail by design the same way once Phase 3 changes
row states. Each phase checker is phase-bound; the final validation rests on the Phase 3 and
Phase 4 checkers plus the doctor. The plan should add the analogous by-design note for
check-review.sh when Phase 3 runs. One of the 90 FAILs (inn says missing but its source exists)
is the Phase 1 F2 substring defect surfacing on the inn MAPS note, not state drift; harmless
inside a by-design failure.

## Findings

No blocking findings. Three nits:

- F1 [Nit] check-review.sh:211-265: P2-d never verifies the Judge critical cell or the judge
  route cell, while plan.md:59 claims the rows hold the judge route and the copied rating,
  critical flag and note. Fixture proof: both mutations pass 34/34. The committed inventory is
  faithful (30 rows, 0 mismatches), so the exposure is future drift. The critical flag feeds
  the Phase 3 rework set (below 7.0 or critical); mill is double-covered (5.5 and true).
- F2 [Nit] check-review.sh:202-208: the model-id grep in the log-citation check is always true
  once the route grep passes, because the route string contains the model id. The test reduces
  to the log contains the route. The committed logs carry explicit model_id lines, so only the
  test label overstates coverage.
- F3 [Nit] The by-design check-inventory.sh failure and its later-gate consequences, described
  above.

